    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104719" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐαγμός</span></b> , ὁ, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐαγμοί</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the triad</i> or
				<i>the triads,</i> a philos. work by Ion of Chios, <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴων</span>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				8.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Clem.Al.
				<u>Strom.</u>
				1.21
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				131
			</span></i> (where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριαγμοῖς</span> is
			restored for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριγράμμοις</span>); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐασμοί</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρφεύς.</span>
			</div>
